[
  {
    "id": "vllm-engine",
    "caption": "vLLM's scheduler re-forms the batch at every step, and PagedAttention hands each request KV-cache blocks on demand, so shared prefixes reuse blocks and memory runs out late instead of early.",
    "alt": "Clients call the OpenAI-compatible API server. Requests enter a waiting queue. At every step the scheduler admits waiting requests and retires finished ones, building a batch that mixes chunked prefill with decode. The model runner executes the batch on the GPU, reading and writing the KV cache, which is divided into fixed-size blocks allocated per request; requests with the same prompt prefix share blocks. If blocks run out, the scheduler preempts a request back to the queue.",
